":"Lennart","familyname":"von Post","contactname":"von Post, Lennart"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Data were digitized from the pollen diagram in Figure 1, von Post (1918). According to the text, the pollen sum included all trees except Corylus, whose percentages were based on the sum of the other types. The raw digitized tree sums, which varied from 94.5-100.5%, were adjusted to sum to 100%. These percentages were multiplied times a pollen sum of 200 to back calculate the counts. The actual pollen sums were not indicated on the pollen diagram or in the text.","recdatecreated":"2019-06-19T21:41:05"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":25895,"sitename":"Rönneholms Mosse","sitedescription":"Raised bog. Currently being mined for peat.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[13.39943,55.91111],[13.44055,55.91111],[13.44055,55.93037],[13.39943,55.93037],[13.39943,55.91111]]]}","altitude":38,"collectionunitid":31678,"collectionunit":"300 m","handle":"RONNHOLB","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/5d23-1196"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":6214,"ageyoung":357}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":44763,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"L.","contactid":15608,"firstname":"Lennart","familyname":"von Post","contactname":"von Post, Lennart"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Data were digitized from the pollen diagram in Figure 1, von Post (1918). According to the text, the pollen sum included all trees except Corylus, whose percentages were based on the sum of the other types. The raw digitized tree sums, which varied from 94.5-100.5%, were adjusted to sum to 100%. These percentages were multiplied times a pollen sum of 200 to back calculate the counts. The actual pollen sums were not indicated on the pollen diagram or in the text.","recdatecreated":"2019-06-22T18:55:26"}]}},{"site":{"siteid":25958,"sitename":"Lerbäcker Moor","sitedescription":"Raised bog and fen on glaciofluvial sands. Much of it already cut for peat in 1916.","sitenotes":null,"geography":"{\"type\":\"Polygon\",\"crs\":{\"type\":\"name\",\"properties\":{\"name\":\"EPSG:4326\"}},\"coordinates\":[[[15.04278,58.94792],[15.0675,58.94792],[15.0675,58.9619],[15.04278,58.9619],[15.04278,58.94792]]]}","altitude":121,"collectionunitid":31806,"collectionunit":"274 m","handle":"LERBAK274","unittype":"Core","datasets":[{"doi":["10.21233/184t-cc14"],"agerange":[{"units":"Calibrated radiocarbon years BP","ageold":7870,"ageyoung":81}],"database":"European Pollen Database","datasetid":44897,"datasetpi":[{"initials":"L.","contactid":15608,"firstname":"Lennart","familyname":"von Post","contactname":"von Post, Lennart"}],"datasettype":"pollen","datasetnotes":"Data were digitized from the pollen diagram in Figure 10, von Post (1916). According to the text, the pollen sum included all trees except Corylus, whose percentages were based on the sum of the other types. The raw digitized percentages were adjusted to sum to100%. The adjusted percentages were used to back calculate the pollen counts using the pollen sums shown on the pollen diagram.","recdatecreated":"2019-06-28T22:43:02"}]}}],"message":"Retrieved all tables"}